# Port block for /etc/mgetty/mgetty.config.
# Paste it into that file. If a "port tnt0" block is already there,
# replace that block and leave every other port alone.
#
# fido-send-emsi y makes mgetty send EMSI_REQ and wait for EMSI_INQ
# before login.config runs qico -a emsi. With it off, a mailer never
# types the login name /FIDO/ and the call falls through to nologin.
#
# PeerHayes answers a bare AT and ATZ with OK. ATZ restores its
# defaults: S0=0 (no auto-answer) and verbose text result codes.
# mgetty then sends ATA itself.
#
# tty0tty wires the peer's DTR to both DSR and DCD. PeerHayes raises
# DTR only while the call is up, so DSR is off during init. need-dsr
# stays n so mgetty still sends AT. ignore-carrier stays n: after
# CONNECT, DCD is real and a dropped DTR ends the line.
# toggle-dtr y lets mgetty reset a modem that is stuck online.

port tnt0
  speed 57600
  data-only y
  toggle-dtr y
  need-dsr n
  ignore-carrier n
  fido-send-emsi y
  issue-file /dev/null
  init-chat "" AT OK ATZ OK
